Design a report generator
-- available in multiple formats - pdf, docx, HTML, etc.,
-- should be able to add new type of reports.
--- sales, user and inventory

-- no tight coupling (loose coupling)

--- Delivery of report -> email, download, blob storage

Abstract Class:
- Report -> sales, user, inventory.
-----> getTitle, getContent, Generate

Report class will take interface type, the extended can dynamically take the format class.

report -> type --- 1:many

Bridge class is used in both report and type.

Interface
- Type -> pdf, docx, HTML
-----> GenerateReport method -> which generates final report.

class SalesReport extends Report{
    public SalesReport(Type type){
        super(type);
    }
}

class PDF implements Type{
    @Override
    public void generateReport(){
        width = 0.5*Type.width;
        content = report.getContent();
    }
}

class TypeFactory(){
    Type getType(String input){
        switch(input){
            case "pdf":
                return new PDF();
            case "docx":
                return new DOCX();
        }
    }
}

Main class
Type type = TypeFactory.getType("pdf");
Report report  = new SalesReport(type);
report.generate();

Association -> both entities can exist independently.
composition -> both depends on each other.
aggregation -> other class can exist independently. (weak relation) (B can exist

